<article class="env-definition" id="0724">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0724">Definition <span data-tag="0724">69.6.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : U \to X$ be a surjective étale morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be an object of $\textit{Ab}(X_{\acute{e}tale})$. The <em>alternating Čech complex</em><a class="footnotemark" href="#a0001383328" id="a0001383328-mark"><sup>1</sup></a> $\check{\mathcal{C}}^\bullet _{alt}(f, \mathcal{F})$ associated to $\mathcal{F}$ and $f$ is the complex </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (K^0, \mathcal{F}) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (K^1, \mathcal{F}) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (K^2, \mathcal{F}) \to \ldots  \]
</div>
  <p> with Hom groups computed in $\textit{Ab}(X_{\acute{e}tale})$. </p>
</article>